# 🟢 Level 1 – Beginner Explanation

## What is a Packet?

When you send a large file over the internet, it isn't sent as one giant block.

Instead, it is divided into **small pieces called packets**.

### 📦 Analogy

Imagine sending a 500-page book by courier.

Instead of one huge package, you divide it into 10 smaller boxes.

Each box has:

* Sender address
* Receiver address
* Page numbers

The receiver reassembles the book.

The Internet works in exactly the same way.

---

# Packet Encapsulation

As data moves down the networking stack, each layer adds its own information (called a **header**).

```text
Application Data
        ↓
TCP Header Added
        ↓
IP Header Added
        ↓
Ethernet Header Added
        ↓
Bits Sent Across Network
```

At the destination, the reverse process (**decapsulation**) removes each header until the original data is recovered.

