# Wireshark

Wireshark is one of the most widely used packet analyzers.

It captures live network traffic so you can inspect packets.

---

## Basic Steps

1. Open Wireshark.
2. Select your active network interface (Wi-Fi or Ethernet).
3. Start capturing.
4. Open a website.
5. Stop the capture.

You will see hundreds of packets. That's normal.

---

## Useful Wireshark Filters

Display only DNS traffic:

```text
dns
```

Only HTTP traffic:

```text
http
```

Only HTTPS traffic:

```text
tls
```

Only ICMP packets:

```text
icmp
```

Only TCP packets:

```text
tcp
```

Only UDP packets:

```text
udp
```

Learning filters is one of the fastest ways to become productive with Wireshark.

